{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate","id":1111587,"title":"Keeping the Game Lines Separate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-05T02:04:07-07:00","id":1111587,"title":"Keeping the Game Lines Separate","content":"It seems like I am always hearing or reading about new and better ways to integrate the World of Darkness, to come up with better crossovers or combine the metaplot to make it all work together. Sometimes I think that I must be the only person out there who likes to keep my game lines entirely separate. When I play Vampire, there is no Technocracy controlling human society and making technology work, there is no Pentex controlling the corporate world and putting Wyrm poison into people's hamburgers. Hell, there may not even be mages or werewolves at all, or they might be much different from how they are depicted in their own game lines. When I play Werewolf, I don't want to deal with the possibility of there being an Abrahamic God who cursed vampires or the idea that Gaia and the Wyrm might just be caused by humans believing this or that. <br /> <br /> I think that the different game lines have not only their own unique flavors and play styles, they have their own settings and cosmologies that are mutually exclusive. Trying to combine them just undermines what make at least one (if not more) of those games special. While I've never been much of a fan of the Ravnos Clan, one of my least things in V:tM was the Week of Nightmares where the Technocracy killed Ravnos with giant space mirrors. <br /> <br /> Am I alone in this regard? Are there other people who feel the same way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T04:14:13-07:00","id":1111607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate#post1111587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that the different game lines have not only their own unique flavors and play styles, they have their own settings and cosmologies that are mutually exclusive. Trying to combine them just undermines what make at least one (if not more) of those games special. While I've never been much of a fan of the Ravnos Clan, one of my least things in V:tM was the Week of Nightmares where the Technocracy killed Ravnos with giant space mirrors. <br /> <br /> Am I alone in this regard? Are there other people who feel the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>No you're not. I also separate the game lines pretty hard, especially when I'm storytelling. <br /> This began as a more practical way because I had severel players who were so in to the different splats, that I just said that I will have my one rake on the different splats while we're playing VtM. So I can do all kind of shenanigans in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T09:45:50-07:00","id":1111686,"title":"","content":"I mostly dabble in Chronicles Of Darkness these days, where that is less of a concern, but when it comes to World Of Darkness I do exactly the same. I take each gameline as its own centerpiece and, while I aknowledge the presence of others, I don't like mixing mythos and setting.<br /> <br /> Makes thing way easier and I also believe it helps to show the strong points of each game. Sometimes I use little elements from other games, like a Giovanni Vampire in a Wraith Game or namedrop Pentex in a Demon game, but it's mostly harmless fanservice that never expands to the setting of gamelines different from the one I'm focusing on.<br /> <br /> The golden rule I have is pretty much &quot;whatever we're looking at right now is the right one&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":"as if that is an odd thing. Brain failure 07-05-2017, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T09:52:36-07:00","id":1111691,"title":"","content":"I, myself, am a huge proponent of keeping the game lines separate. I don't like the feeling at all that they could be in the same continuity. Now I will throw random references in different game lines to kind of give the feel of continuity, but it is usually mortal NPCS. For example, I mentioned a mortal motorcycle club in passing in my Chronicles of Darkness game, that was in a Vampire: the Masquerade game I ran. Just in passing, not involved in the plot or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T11:18:16-07:00","id":1111729,"title":"","content":"I'm actually the opposite and believe a living world needs to show the entire world. So while I would never allow the PCs to be crossover (no groups of werewolves with one changeling, or a group of vampires plus one mage, etc.), their setting contains everything. At the same time, I have a very edited version of canon so I don't include every ridiculous thing out there.<br /> <br /> I do give a lot of thought about what kind of other game elements are around and could be possibly interacted with. Most of my Chronicles the PCs never encounter the easter eggs I put there, and I never have a major plot element or story where those other game elements are driving things.<br /> <br /> The main reason is I want to have a sense of &quot;there are dragons out there&quot; in the PCs minds so they realize some sections of the map are out of their control, or no-go zones, or simply have some things be very mysterious. I like a sandbox style game, and part of the sandbox needs to be these other areas. Especially if one or more PC is in a very occult oriented character, I want them to realize that there are many other occult forces out there as well.<br /> <br /> When I run a game, I try to include the following:<br /> <br /> A general sandbox that the PCs can run around and explore<br /> Elements specific to each PC because of their backgrounds and interests, catered to them<br /> One general chronicle wide mystery which they may or may not get involved<br /> <br /> I think this layered approach keeps the game fun and fresh giving the illusion of a real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:36:37-07:00","id":1111817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate#post1111587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I alone in this regard? Are there other people who feel the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're not. Some people, like me like the modern-urban-fnatasy-kitchen-sink approach of crossovers (which, I firmly believe even started largely with WoD), because more things could make the setting more colorful. Others like complete separation, for thematic pureness, or other reasons, or any point between those extremes. It's all good, chill! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:44:55-07:00","id":1111820,"title":"","content":"I think maybe I have a middle ground approach. When I run a game, I generally assume that some elements of the other games are still around (there's probably a Camarilla for example, the Technocracy is fartzing around, Garou are protecting Caerns/Nodes and so on), but I don't go into very much detail unless my players specifically want to deal with other supernatural types. <br /> <br /> I prefer to keep the focus, player characters, and cosmology specific to the game I'm running (no Triat in Vampire, for example), but I like having the hint of a wider universe. If nothing else, it can make for a fun change of pace. If the mages are getting tired of exploring the Umbra, they can end up in a political conflict with a Vampire for a bit of novelty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:24:30-07:00","id":1111837,"title":"","content":"I always use the one World of Darkness approach (though I have the discrepancies of MtAs caused by perceptual distortions originating from the paradigm lens maintained by their Avatars and of DtF caused by the vulnerability of Demons to mortal beliefs). I like using Garou and KJ to terrify Kindred and everything to terrify Mages. It is also fun creating the complex framework of supernatural politics within a place like NY state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T23:16:28-07:00","id":1112522,"title":"","content":"You hear a lot about resolving crossovers in online discussions because it presents a lot of difficult challenges, whereas running the games as totally standalone is sort of the default state for which they were originally written (canon crossover books notwithstanding). Personally, I'm running a full-on crossover game, but if I were running one of the games individually I probably would keep the other lines mostly out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13544-impeesa","name":"Impeesa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T05:38:39-07:00","id":1112614,"title":"","content":"You can have a crossover setting without having crossover games. It just gives you more options, but you do not have to use everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:29:38-07:00","id":1112843,"title":"","content":"At this point if I want to run a game with lots of crossover, I'd run CofD instead of WoD. Unlike WoD, CofD is actually written to accommodate it.<br /> <br /> If I run WoD, there'll probably be some crossover but I'm more likely to keep the other game lines within the context of the game line I am primarily running. So lupines instead of Garou in Vampire, leeches instead of Kindred in Werewolf, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T17:35:24-07:00","id":1113005,"title":"","content":"I acknowledge the existence of the other splats but don't use most of their cannon. Nor do I use many of their factions. For example I only use Ventrue, Toreador, and Tzimisce of the vampire clans and werewolves are just werewolves. Of course I don't play werewolf so that's that. I do incorporate the Fae but not really their politics.<br /> <br /> Edit: Forgot which Forum I was in. I run Mage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T13:19:23-07:00","id":1113347,"title":"","content":"I I do use elements from other gamelines when they make things interesting, but usually, I keep them separate and my groups are always segregated. (I once played a Vampire in a Mage game, since I couldn't get my mind around the magic system. God, you feel useless...). What I did do in a longer Vampire game was use Pentex as a main antagonist. It's just so useful. Their Fomori are a visceral threat, their money and power is a threat to the higher-ups financial interests and nothing creeps vampires more out than dropping a line like. &quot;Maybe that girl ate something weird, because her blood tastes... unclean&quot;<br /> Otherwise, I take my players wishes into consideration. Like, one of my regulars was really into Promethian for a while, so I thought I could do him a favour and just throw one in for fun. <br /> Basically, stuff exists, but you only find it if you look for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T14:50:08-07:00","id":1113393,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if anyone was going to mention the Fractured Cosmos from <b>Ascension</b>: the \u201cWorld\u201d of Darkness consists of several parallel worlds that echo each other. Each world puts one gameline and its metaphysics front and center, with elements of the other gamelines manifesting within the rules of that world's cosmos if at all. Big events in a given world (such as <b>Vampire</b>'s Week of Nightmares) tend to resonate with other worlds, causing similar events to occur; but for the most part, each world does its own thing. Likewise, the monsters on each world echo the world where they're central; but they're not the <i>same</i>: the lupines of <b>Vampire</b> are not the Garou of <b>Werewolf</b>, despite superficial similarities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T15:54:19-07:00","id":1113430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1113393#post1113393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if anyone was going to mention the Fractured Cosmos from <b>Ascension</b>: the \u201cWorld\u201d of Darkness consists of several parallel worlds that echo each other. Each world puts one gameline and its metaphysics front and center, with elements of the other gamelines manifesting within the rules of that world's cosmos if at all. Big events in a given world (such as <b>Vampire</b>'s Week of Nightmares) tend to resonate with other worlds, causing similar events to occur; but for the most part, each world does its own thing. Likewise, the monsters on each world echo the world where they're central; but they're not the <i>same</i>: the lupines of <b>Vampire</b> are not the Garou of <b>Werewolf</b>, despite superficial similarities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this described because dang is it similar to an approach I had at one point.<br /> <br /> I mean do you mean Mage: The Ascension in general or <b>Ascension</b>, the Time of Judgment book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T17:43:39-07:00","id":1113467,"title":"","content":"The <b>Time of Judgment</b> book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T00:06:17-07:00","id":1113631,"title":"","content":"Many things really feel mutually exclusive. How can there be wererats in the same world as the nosferatu? How can there be bonegnawers in the same world where vampires routinely feed on the homeless? In a vampire game, wererats have to be nonexistent or at least extraordinarily rare. Werewolves are purely creatures of small towns and the woods.<br /> <br /> Conversely, in a werewolf game vampires are rare creatures who exist almost entirely in the realm of the super-rich, penthouses, corporate boardrooms, the modern equivalent of lords in their castles so far removed from the daily peasants that a werewolf would rarely even glimpse them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T02:42:20-07:00","id":1113665,"title":"","content":"I am reading about the &quot;Fractured Cosmos&quot; crossover concept in the Ascension book that Dataweaver mentioned just now, and..wow. Why have I never noticed that section?<br /> <br /> It's neat. It's kind of really really neat. I'd love to quote the whole shebang because it has so many neat ideas, but that'd just not be proper.<br /> I'll cherry pick a couple that I think are the essence:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The destinies of these worlds are intertwined. When<br /> a significant event occurs in one, its vibrations transmit<br /> to the others. Sometimes, this causes the parallel uni-<br /> verse to duplicate the event, but precise details shift. A<br /> sufficiently strong pulse can violate causality in several<br /> universes. The events of the Reckoning might have<br /> been so traumatic that cause and effect were scrambled,<br /> allowing the Ravnos Ancient to project its singular be-<br /> ing into several worlds. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it possible to travel to alternate Worlds of Dark-<br /> ness? Spirit, Correspondence, Time and Entropy magic<br /> could all help catapult a mage into another world. &lt;...&gt;<br /> Characters might be able to reach alternate worlds<br /> through the Umbra, but only by traveling past the Outer<br /> Horizon and into uncharted Umbral space. In the spiritual<br /> wilderness, the traveler needs to search for paths that don\u2019t<br /> correspond with physical space. Rumor has it that great<br /> cracks and portals lie in the deepest regions of Umbra,<br /> capable of taking voyagers out of the known Tapestry<br /> completely. Parallel worlds include their own Umbrae<br /> all the way to the Outer Horizon. Even the spirit world<br /> can change from universe to universe. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the default Fractured Cosmos, we assume<br /> that the universes described in each game line are<br /> sufficiently entangled that people and objects can\u2019t<br /> duplicate themselves. A technomancer who changes<br /> her quantum harmonics to visit the world described in<br /> Vampire displaces her counterpart. Her counterpart will<br /> be almost exactly the same, but a few slight differences<br /> might arouse suspicion in her friends. Remember that<br /> according to this model, moving between universes is<br /> common. Most people aren\u2019t even aware of it, since the<br /> Tapestries tend to have very subtle differences. </div> </div> </div>It then desribes that the duplicate, instead of being superimposed, might also subtly shift into another variant without noticing.<br /> And it the writeup goes on to describe versions of the universe(s) with alternate history - one where the Reckoning happened in 1000 AD for example.<br /> What I really, really like about this approach is that, not only does it handle the incompatible differences between the gamelines with elegance - it also creates new story opportunities in the very same writeup. My hat is off to that, because usually any variants of gameline separation tends to reduce those instead. I really really like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T06:17:09-07:00","id":1113703,"title":"","content":"Yes, it is an optional rule in the chapter on designing your own end of the world in a non-canon book. It says that you can treat every gameline as a separate universe, not that it is the default for MtAs or oWoD. If you read the section before it, you will notice that they discuss how to deal with the default assumption, the unified oWoD. In any case, the default assumption is a unified oWoD, though no one is forcing anyone to play multiple gamelines together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T06:45:00-07:00","id":1113710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1113703#post1113703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it is an optional rule in the chapter on designing your own end of the world in a non-canon book. It says that you can treat every gameline as a separate universe, not that it is the default for MtAs or oWoD. If you read the section before it, you will notice that they discuss how to deal with the default assumption, the unified oWoD. In any case, the default assumption is a unified oWoD, though no one is forcing anyone to play multiple gamelines together.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>A Unified World of Darkness</b><br /> <br /> Paring down the setting will help you take care of<br /> <b>major contradictions</b>, but you still need to wrestle with<br /> divergent histories and street-level metaphysics, like<br /> the eternal question of why werewolves and vampires<br /> can avoid Paradox.<br /> <b>There\u2019s no easy answer. Each game was designed to be<br /> true to itself first.</b> </div> </div> </div>The default assumption seems to be that it's a contradictory mess, with each game line written for itself.<br /> The TL;DR of the suggestions is to take the gameline you want to run, and try to make the rest fit into it. As usual. There is no 'single' unified oWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T11:43:00-07:00","id":1113800,"title":"","content":"I've always ran my masquerade games as standalone lines, and I made use of the various Hunters Hunted numina for mage type characters while I used the different disciplines to do lupine type characters.<br /> <br /> However, I've never run each gameline being true in one world because I could never keep track of who was supposed to be puppeteering who; however, I like that fractured cosmos idea. I'll have to make use of that at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T11:48:55-07:00","id":1113803,"title":"","content":"I like the fractured cosmos thing because it suggests that the World of Darkness is fundamentally <i>broken</i> on a cosmological level. That this cluster of Worlds of Darkness is a kind of aberration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:31:00-07:00","id":1115259,"title":"","content":"Well, if I do have a cross-over, I tend to run it as if it were part of the game; a mage in VtM would be a hedge-magician and use the Sorcerer book for spells and for a werewolf, I just derive stats from V:tM. Certain things are not crossed-over such as WoD and V:tm; basically, I view this, &quot;OWoD = V:tM&quot; or purposes of rules etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T01:12:13-08:00","id":1172946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1113631#post1113631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many things really feel mutually exclusive. How can there be wererats in the same world as the nosferatu? How can there be bonegnawers in the same world where vampires routinely feed on the homeless? In a vampire game, wererats have to be nonexistent or at least extraordinarily rare. Werewolves are purely creatures of small towns and the woods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you really think that when a Nosferatu warren gets wiped out that the Nicktuku were behind it? They've spent most of the last few thousand years in torpor like the rest of the inhabitants of the 2nd city. <br /> <br /> Conversely, do you really think the Nosferatu were only feeding on &quot;rats&quot; down there? It doesn't make logistical sense unless the rats are bigger than you'd expect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T05:01:18-08:00","id":1172968,"title":"","content":"The story behind the games works differently depending on which one you're running. If you're running a crossover they all have to adjust to accomodate the others. That isn't terribly difficult unless you have people pedantically pointing out that the books have stuff in them that doesn't agree.<br /> <br /> Far more troublesome in my view is picking out which archetypes come from where. The stories aren't hard to mix but I find you want to either limit an archetype to one supernatural type or have a game that's mostly around one or two complementary archetypes. Basically you need characters that don't step on each other. In a game with five players for example you wouldn't want to see a malkavian, a troll and a brujah. The latter two would step on each other while the first two wouldn't. If everyone's the same or similar archetype (ahroun, troll, brujah, redcap for example) then what type of supernatural they are tends to separate them out because in this example, you can focus on a pretty physical game. They can just be different approaches to it. But if you're balancing social and mental as well it's much more difficult to add enough nuance to one area. That makes it too easy to end up with one of the PCs just being clearly superior at their specialty. Which definitely doesn't make for a good game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23656-lanir","name":"Lanir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T13:34:45-08:00","id":1173072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1172946#post1172946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you really think that when a Nosferatu warren gets wiped out that the Nicktuku were behind it? They've spent most of the last few thousand years in torpor like the rest of the inhabitants of the 2nd city.<br /> <br /> Conversely, do you really think the Nosferatu were only feeding on &quot;rats&quot; down there? It doesn't make logistical sense unless the rats are bigger than you'd expect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking logistical inconsistencies, how do the Nosferatu even fit down there unless they're all in mist form? Sewers aren't actually spacious homes in the waiting like in TMNT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T18:15:14-08:00","id":1173121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1173072#post1173072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we're talking logistical inconsistencies, how do the Nosferatu even fit down there unless they're all in mist form? Sewers aren't actually spacious homes in the waiting like in TMNT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Storm drains tend to be quite large. Then you have old train and subway tunnels. And that's in modern North American real world cities. I'm sure the Nos pay contractors to build annexes that are quickly forgotten about whenever the above systems are expanded.<br /> <br /> And in Europe you have underground canals, catacombs, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T23:01:33-08:00","id":1173167,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> <br /> I've gone spelunking in Adelaide, Australia, which is pretty new as far as countries go, and there are plenty of places that could be blocked off as a haven.<br /> With a bit of supernatural strength, I'm sure that I could mine additional caverns with blocked-passage doors; or enter a basement<br /> With resources and contacts, or even just the right know how, you could have basements installed in new homes, open them to the sewers and remove access to the main house (Then Sell the house without advertising it's basement history)<br /> In sewer/stormwater development stages, ghouled workers could extend areas as well.<br /> <br /> Heck you've got me plotting the underground design just thinking about it.<br /> <br /> The thing with Nos and Ratkin specifically, is both have stealth skills/powers and most don't really have the power to see through the other's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T09:07:56-08:00","id":1173235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1173167#post1173167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a><br /> I've gone spelunking in Adelaide, Australia, which is pretty new as far as countries go, and there are plenty of places that could be blocked off as a haven.<br /> With a bit of supernatural strength, I'm sure that I could mine additional caverns with blocked-passage doors; or enter a basement</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem there is that the WoD likes to place a lot of sanity-shattering gribblies in cave systems. If it's not the Dancers setting up a Hive, it's something like Vhujunka doing their Lovecraftian monster thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With resources and contacts, or even just the right know how, you could have basements installed in new homes, open them to the sewers and remove access to the main house (Then Sell the house without advertising it's basement history)<br /> In sewer/stormwater development stages, ghouled workers could extend areas as well.<br /> <br /> Heck you've got me plotting the underground design just thinking about it.<br /> <br /> The thing with Nos and Ratkin specifically, is both have stealth skills/powers and most don't really have the power to see through the other's. </div> </div> </div>That seems like a tremendous threat to secrecy if you do it more than once or twice. People catch wind of all of the underground construction directly opening up into the sewer, and they're likely to become suspicious about why that is.<br /> <br /> Also, the Ratkin can peer in from the Umbra and see the vampires as dark blotches, even if they're using Obfuscate. The Nosferatu cannot really return the favor in a comparable fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T14:27:27-08:00","id":1173327,"title":"","content":"I did not know the Ratkin had that, it does seem like something that makes total cross over difficult (in that area)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T18:02:29-08:00","id":1173385,"title":"","content":"If I'm running a game then my focus is on that game. However. I will take elements from other games to use as I require, so there is a Camarilla and a Sabbat and Anarchs when I'm running Werewolf or Mage but odds are I give them little consideration unless it impacts on the story or character actions. The same in any other combination too, my Technocracy is monolithic and controls much but is far from as omniescent as my players feel when they are playing Mage than when they are Camarilla neonates. I also tend to reuse a few settings like the fictional cities of Severnford and Hecates Peace with some reoccurring NPCs and events of previous stories and chronicles also colouring the setting in later games. Actual crossover happens infrequently and then in the form of antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T07:16:47-08:00","id":1174268,"title":"","content":"I run games in a unfied WoD but as the different supernaturals naturally tend to avoid each other crossings are not necessarily that common but they do happen. Technocracy for example exists in all my games and if things get too outofhand they will take action but in like is said on the Guide to the Technocracy they normally trust the Vampires to govern themselves for example and due to high inherent Banality they mostly believe Fae to be extinct Etc. So they focus on the most dangerous reality deviants out there like traditionalists and Nephandi and only come down on the others if they get to out of hand.<br /> <br /> Personally I really cannot fathom the \u201dseperate lines\u201d line of thought since the Tremere are directly from Mage, as are Nagaraja, Fianna are related to the Fae, House Fiona is related to the Garou while the head of House Balor has BSD bodyguards, Silent Striders (and many other Egyptian shifters) are in a holy war against the Setites Etc. There are several more examples of such rather official connections between the lines so I feel any claim for the lines to be seperate requires a huge amount of suspencion of disbelief to work. But like it often is with these things YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T13:43:15-08:00","id":1174354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1174268#post1174268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I run games in a unfied WoD but as the different supernaturals naturally tend to avoid each other crossings are not necessarily that common but they do happen. Technocracy for example exists in all my games and if things get too outofhand they will take action but in like is said on the Guide to the Technocracy they normally trust the Vampires to govern themselves for example and due to high inherent Banality they mostly believe Fae to be extinct Etc. So they focus on the most dangerous reality deviants out there like traditionalists and Nephandi and only come down on the others if they get to out of hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the TU doesn't exist in other games, because technology is never treated as magic outside of Mage. They would have no reason to exist as they do in M:tA; the entire setup of the cosmology doesn't agree with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally I really cannot fathom the \u201dseperate lines\u201d line of thought since the Tremere are directly from Mage, as are Nagaraja, Fianna are related to the Fae, House Fiona is related to the Garou while the head of House Balor has BSD bodyguards, Silent Striders (and many other Egyptian shifters) are in a holy war against the Setites Etc. There are several more examples of such rather official connections between the lines so I feel any claim for the lines to be seperate requires a huge amount of suspencion of disbelief to work. But like it often is with these things YMMV. </div> </div> </div>Any claim that the lines aren't separate has to deal with the writing and construction of each game ignoring the others to do their own respective things. This, as always, is present most notably between Mage and Werewolf, but it's not like Vampire and Demon really play well with Werewolf or Mage, either, what without any access to the same spiritual world that the Garou and Fera are slipping into. The only game that can slot into any of the others is Hunter, and that's because the Imbued are all written as confused babes in the woods who don't know what's going on and the OOC stuff never really gives concrete answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T18:01:23-08:00","id":1174416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the TU doesn't exist in other games, because technology is never treated as magic outside of Mage. They would have no reason to exist as they do in M:tA; the entire setup of the cosmology doesn't agree with it. </div> </div> </div>Technology in mage is treated as magic, as in handled with rules for magic, when it is beyond currently available technology which is not available in other lines, as it is mostly in hands of the TU, except for wherewolf where there is a certain amount of weaver tech present and that certainly is magical, and in fact magical in a way accepted by Mages as well, since it is powered by weaver spirits. So basically technological fetishes. Which is available tech in mage as well.<br /> <br /> So absense of magical technology in a manual for creatures who are in majority of circumstances unable to use them, due to lacking an Awakened Avatar, is hardly proof that the lines are seperate. Especially since so many things, as I have already given plenty of examples of, tie the lines rather strongly together. Antediluvian Set drove an entire tribe of Garou of their land and cursed them unable to return for example. Week of Nightmares had the Technocratic Union assault an awakened antediluvian vampire in a chain of events that almost wiped a whole clan of the face of the earth. Their spirit nukes destroyed the local dreamscape releasing the Naraka Dark-kin upon the Autumn lands reborn without their memories. Quote grand effects from an organization that doesn\u2019t apparently exist in any of the aforementioned affected lines, is it not.<br /> <br /> But if you are not content to accept fluff or IC sources as convincing evidence of a unified WoD there are OOC evidence as well. For example Dark Ages: Werewolf, Mage, Fae and Inquisitors all declare right there in their back cover that they require Dark Ages: Vampire to use, which basically makes them sourcebooks for Dark Ages: Vampire.<br /> <br /> Also Mummy the Resurrection needs another lines main book to use, and it\u2019s antagonists are mostly feomthe other lines as were it\u2019s predecessors as well.<br /> <br /> Every table does things their way, has their own House rules and likely affect the metaplot in different and unique ways if they even use the metaplot at all or just as bacground fluff of the past. Like said YMMV. Still I, personally, feel the lines to be so strongly connected that to claim otherwise is going to House rule territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T18:04:48-08:00","id":1174419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1174354#post1174354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Any claim that the lines aren't separate has to deal with the writing and construction of each game ignoring the others to do their own respective things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And any claim that the lines are separate must explain why Rage across Russia, Rage across New York, Rage across Amazonia, Nights of the Prophecy, Times of Thin Blood, Blood Treachery, the Book of Chantries,Dark Alliance Vancouver,Valkenburg Foundation,New Orleans by Night, Washington DC by Night,Midnight Circus,Under a Blood Red Moon,Book of the Wyrm,Apocalypse, Ascension, Project Twilight,Guide to the Tecnocracy,Euthanatos revised, The Horizon War triology. the Book of Madness, Masters of the Arts (and more or less all KOTE and Wraith) are all written on the premise that all these worlds are one, interconnected at their deepest core.<br /> <br /> <br /> Truth is, if someone wants to discard the other game lines he has to discard half of the pubblications of each splats, beacuse besides the corebooks and the tribes/clan/Tradition books every other published things has the one world of darkness as necessary premise.<br /> <br /> Otherwise one should explain why the Tremere of Blood Treachery is not the Tremere of Vampire, or why the Technocracy of Rage across the Amazon is not the Technocracy of mage, or why the Baba Yaga of Times of thin blood is not the same of Rage Across Russia, or why the Nephandi of Midnight Circus are not the Nephandi of Ascension, or why the Camarilla of Guide to Technocracy is not the same of the one in Guide to the Camarilla, or why the Sabbat in Rage across New York is not the same sabbat of Washington Dc by Night or why the Maeljin Incarna in the Horizon War triology is not the same maeljin incarna of werewolf and so on.<br /> <br /> So if at your table they are separate game lines that's fine, no one can say anything about an house rule. That said canon is: the world is one..<br /> <br /> <br /> And not just because I say so, but because White Wolf, who own the creative rights on these IPs has decided so. You can disagree with them, but since they own the IP rights it's them that must choose what is true and what is not true, and they decided the the lines are merged in one world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?time_continue=1341&amp;v=sEoG8YQrLuE\" data-code=\"sEoG8YQrLuE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/sEoG8YQrLuE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-08-2018, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T19:10:01-08:00","id":1174432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1174419#post1174419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And any claim that the lines are separate must explain why Rage across Russia, Rage across New York, Rage across Amazonia, Nights of the Prophecy, Times of Thin Blood, Blood Treachery, the Book of Chantries,Dark Alliance Vancouver,Valkenburg Foundation,New Orleans by Night, Washington DC by Night,Midnight Circus,Under a Blood Red Moon,Book of the Wyrm,Apocalypse, Ascension, Project Twilight,Guide to the Tecnocracy,Euthanatos revised, The Horizon War triology. the Book of Madness, Masters of the Arts (and more or less all KOTE and Wraith) are all written on the premise that all these worlds are one, interconnected at their deepest core.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are all written for a particular game and tend to ignore parts of the other game or games that don't fit. It's common practice, required for any crossover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Truth is, if someone wants to discard the other game lines he has to discard half of the pubblications of each splats, beacuse besides the corebooks and the tribes/clan/Tradition books every other published things has the one world of darkness as necessary premise.<br /> <br /> Otherwise one should explain why the Tremere of Blood Treachery is not the Tremere of Vampire, or why the Technocracy of Rage across the Amazon is not the Technocracy of mage, or why the Baba Yaga of Times of thin blood is not the same of Rage Across Russia, or why the Nephandi of Midnight Circus are not the Nephandi of Ascension, or why the Camarilla of Guide to Technocracy is not the same of the one in Guide to the Camarilla, or why the Sabbat in Rage across New York is not the same sabbat of Washington Dc by Night or why the Maeljin Incarna in the Horizon War triology is not the same maeljin incarna of werewolf and so on.<br /> <br /> So if at your table they are separate game lines that's fine, no one can say anything about an house rule. That said canon is: the world is one. </div> </div> </div>Certainly not in Revised. The 20th Anniversary editions didn't walk back all that much from it, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And not just because I say so, but because White Wolf, who own the creative rights on these IPs has decided so. You can disagree with them, but since they own the IP rights it's them that must choose what is true and what is not true, and they decided the the lines are merged in one world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?time_continue=1341&amp;v=sEoG8YQrLuE\" data-code=\"sEoG8YQrLuE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/sEoG8YQrLuE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div> </div> </div> </div>The Storyteller's Handbooks for Revised disagree flat out; for Werewolf's piece on why it doesn't get along with Mage, see page 199 of its respective ST Handbook title, and keep reading. It quite plainly uses the term &quot;in strictest Werewolf cosmology&quot;, implying that, line by line, they're each separate settings unto their own. The crossover section in general starts on page 195 and also touches on having to change a lot of things if you're going for different moods from different games, like reducing the chances of Garou frenzying and killing their friends in a somewhat lighter (or, at the very least, less brutal) Changeling game<br /> <br /> Also, nuWW is making a setting that probably isn't going to resemble what was in past books very much. They've stated their intention to break apart canon and declare past events as &quot;unreliable narration&quot;, and that's ultimately what you have to do to weld disparate games together - break apart or ignore anything that contradicts, make choices about what is and isn't right. That does not end up as a single, intelligible canon setting. That's a collection of elements with some assembly required. Not as much as GURPS, perhaps, but the more you add on, the more time it takes to construct a group's setting, and the less you'll find yourself actually using. Even nuWW can't fit consensus reality with animistic reality together, no matter what magic words of god it tries to invoke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T00:22:47-08:00","id":1174489,"title":"","content":"I'm in the crowd that heavily separates the game lines from each other. Otherwise you will, in no time, end up where a normal human being is the most rare of all creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T11:12:04-08:00","id":1174593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1174489#post1174489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in the crowd that heavily separates the game lines from each other. Otherwise you will, in no time, end up where a normal human being is the most rare of all creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>XDXDXD <br /> <br /> In all fairness, that can happen with one splat too...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T11:41:17-08:00","id":1174602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1174593#post1174593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> XDXDXD<br /> <br /> In all fairness, that can happen with one splat too...</div> </div> </div> </div>True that! But I still think that with just one splat you've got some sense of control over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T11:45:20-08:00","id":1174605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1174602#post1174602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True that! But I still think that with just one splat you've got some sense of control over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Up until psychics and hedge wizards start trying to squeeze in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-09-2018, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T19:49:33-08:00","id":1174743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1174432#post1174432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;in strictest Werewolf cosmology&quot;, implying that</div> </div> </div> </div>Dictionary definition of Cosmology (well, Wikipedia definition) is that it is a body of beliefs. Not the facts of creation. As such, conflicting cosmologies; just like conflicting beliefs, do not negate each other. The &quot;Truth&quot; likely lies somewhere in between.<br /> <br /> Even if it were the facts; we can have exclusively contradicting facts both being true in this setting. Because there's magic.<br /> <br /> And that is the main problem with putting all the core creatures together; the books state things as facts from the perspective of that game line, but there are contradictions if you take things that another game line says is the truth. <br /> Since the reality deals with beings who can literally change and shape reality; we've got to understand that two opposing facts can feasibly both be true, even when they contradict each other.<br /> <br /> There can be the Abrahamic God creating the world 6000 years ago, starting with Adam and Eve (And a very naughty Caine) while it simultaneously was created billions of years ago in the big bang. In a world of Magic/Magick anything is possible.<br /> <br /> Even in game information on who is controling things (eg moles and agents in the FBI etc) that's not impossible to rectify; if someone is corruptible, they're probably open to being a double agent. They may not know they're an agent for some or all of those areas.<br /> <br /> The problem with combining game lines is that the rules don't play with each other too well, how do you do difficulty of someones rage when they don't have it (for instance) Can countermagic work against gifts or disciplines?<br /> <br /> The other problem is processing power of the GM's Brain - trying to factor out what one city is doing with one splat is hard enough, try adding in the whole universe of supernaturals; and your ST will burn out. Or, if they can manage it, the focus drops off the PCs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T22:11:29-08:00","id":1174772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1174743#post1174743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dictionary definition of Cosmology (well, Wikipedia definition) is that it is a body of beliefs. Not the facts of creation. As such, conflicting cosmologies; just like conflicting beliefs, do not negate each other. The &quot;Truth&quot; likely lies somewhere in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dictionaries won't save you. RPG usage of the term means &quot;the way the campaign setting is&quot;. Otherwise, they wouldn't have spent dozens of books talking about how the world works as factual, 0th rule of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if it were the facts; we can have exclusively contradicting facts both being true in this setting. Because there's magic. </div> </div> </div>I don't think it works that way. The ST Handbooks didn't seem to, either, because in Revised, everything got much more rigid... thankfully. I slogged through years of Vampire and Mage being used as clubs before I found out that no, the mega-crossover isn't the way you're supposed to play and no, I was not weird for chafing at having to include considerations of some bizarre orbital prison for Crowleyian types or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=obkm4J-mmOc\" target=\"_blank\">what god thinks</a> when the only thing that I signed on for was animistic werebeasts, free from all of the pointless teasing and half-measures of Shadowrun's way of dealing with animism, magic, and alternate forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that is the main problem with putting all the core creatures together; the books state things as facts from the perspective of that game line, but there are contradictions if you take things that another game line says is the truth.<br /> Since the reality deals with beings who can literally change and shape reality; we've got to understand that two opposing facts can feasibly both be true, even when they contradict each other.<br /> <br /> There can be the Abrahamic God creating the world 6000 years ago, starting with Adam and Eve (And a very naughty Caine) while it simultaneously was created billions of years ago in the big bang. In a world of Magic/Magick anything is possible.<br /> <br /> Even in game information on who is controling things (eg moles and agents in the FBI etc) that's not impossible to rectify; if someone is corruptible, they're probably open to being a double agent. They may not know they're an agent for some or all of those areas. </div> </div> </div>The assumptions that you draw here are utterly alien to me. I don't pay money to buy books so that they can maybe or maybe not provide a campaign setting. I generally assume that what's in the books holds, and that they're not some elaborate gaslighting attempt to pull one over on everyone. Where contradictions occur, it's because people threw something together that sounded interesting at the time, or occasionally because someone is throwing a not quite official bone to people who went out of the way to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QZg8E72xXFA\" target=\"_blank\">buy all of the books</a>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem with combining game lines is that the rules don't play with each other too well, how do you do difficulty of someones rage when they don't have it (for instance) Can countermagic work against gifts or disciplines? </div> </div> </div>The mechanics were never really the problem (excepting, of course, Vampire's continued insistence on Discipline = every other power or Rank, which is like rounding pi to 5). They are, in fact, the easiest, and perhaps only thing that you can make equivalences between. It's the mood of the game that you're trying to play that's the dealbreaker; where the game starts, what it contains, and where it's going to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other problem is processing power of the GM's Brain - trying to factor out what one city is doing with one splat is hard enough, try adding in the whole universe of supernaturals; and your ST will burn out. Or, if they can manage it, the focus drops off the PCs </div> </div> </div>That's another good reason for not including everything written, albeit, as noted, secondary to how you're basically already saved the trouble. If everything works like it says exactly in Werewolf, you won't be focusing on any themes of Mage, at all, and likely nothing from Vampire or Demon, either. There's a sharply limited number of degrees of freedom at work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T16:45:09-08:00","id":1175015,"title":"","content":"Sigh... So this debate literally refuses to die.<br /> <br /> Keeping the lines separate is fine.<br /> <br /> Using WoD as a shared world is fine.<br /> <br /> The books give material for either (but I believe <i>on average</i> they're favoring the later). Players have preferences, <i>writers</i> have preferences. It's cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-10-2018, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T17:36:25-08:00","id":1175031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1175015#post1175015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh... So this debate literally refuse to die.<br /> <br /> Keeping the lines separate is fine.<br /> <br /> Using WoD as a shared world is fine.<br /> <br /> The books give material for either (but I believe <i>on average</i> they're favoring the later). Players have preferences, <i>writers</i> have preferences. It's cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This This This This This This<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T18:04:45-08:00","id":1175044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1174772#post1174772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RPG usage of the term means &quot;the way the campaign setting is&quot;. Otherwise, they wouldn't have spent dozens of books talking about how the world works as factual, 0th rule of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're seeing the same thing from different perspectives. What I'm saying, is that from the perspective of Werewolves; their cosmology is 100% correct, but a mage's perspective has a different truth, and both can be right at the same time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The assumptions that you draw here are utterly alien to me. I don't pay money to buy books so that they can maybe or maybe not provide a campaign setting. I generally assume that what's in the books holds, and that they're not some elaborate gaslighting attempt to pull one over on everyone. Where contradictions occur, it's because people threw something together that sounded interesting at the time, or occasionally because someone is throwing a not quite official bone to people who went out of the way to buy all of the books </div> </div> </div>Yes, from an out of game perspective, sometimes things are thrown together, sometimes they aren't, or can't be thought out thoroughly from the perspective of all game lines and all existing stories. Also, no one has ever had the page count to put together comprehensive rules (Eg a book on disciplines and how each level affects different game lines or NPCs without that stat that is apparently rolled in resistance or contributes to the difficulty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's another good reason for not including everything written, albeit, as noted, secondary to how you're basically already saved the trouble. If everything works like it says exactly in Werewolf, you won't be focusing on any themes of Mage, at all, and likely nothing from Vampire or Demon, either. There's a sharply limited number of degrees of freedom at work. </div> </div> </div>[/QUOTE]<br /> In one game, I agree, it's impossible to cover all the themes successfully while giving them enough attention. From a worldframe; just look at reality - People in poverty striken areas versus the top of the corporate jungle, the day to day life, the &quot;Themes&quot; that they go through are completely different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T19:35:27-08:00","id":1175062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1175044#post1175044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're seeing the same thing from different perspectives. What I'm saying, is that from the perspective of Werewolves; their cosmology is 100% correct, but a mage's perspective has a different truth, and both can be right at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Werewolf is 100% incompatible with Mage. Mage's conception of the cosmos is the exact opposite of what you find in Werewolf. You pick one or the other, and the one you don't pick ends up eating it..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, from an out of game perspective, sometimes things are thrown together, sometimes they aren't, or can't be thought out thoroughly from the perspective of all game lines and all existing stories. </div> </div> </div>The metatext is all that matters here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, no one has ever had the page count to put together comprehensive rules (Eg a book on disciplines and how each level affects different game lines or NPCs without that stat that is apparently rolled in resistance or contributes to the difficulty. </div> </div> </div>Again, extensive crossover rules would be easier and likely less demanding of word count than you think. It takes maybe two or three tables and a few pages worth of considerations to eliminate most of the mechanical problems that presently exist. However, page length for trying to combine Werewolf and Mage is irrelevant; they're immiscible fluids.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In one game, I agree, it's impossible to cover all the themes successfully while giving them enough attention. From a worldframe; just look at reality - People in poverty striken areas versus the top of the corporate jungle, the day to day life, the &quot;Themes&quot; that they go through are completely different. </div> </div> </div>Themes in fictional settings tend to be far more influential, because they tend to cast how the setting is observed and, to a large extent, what is true. In real life, there is no narrative bumper, though we can confidently say that the people at the top of the corporate jungle are, in all likelihood, huge assholes..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T15:58:02-08:00","id":1177443,"title":"","content":"from a vampire's perspective, werewolf and mage work very well. I think the outliers with werewolf are possessed and gnawers. Ratkin take up little space and can be handwaved by nosferatu keeping away from certain areas of the sewers. Gnawers are a problem, but they're rare and have some strict policies. I would suspect that the awareness talent would be very useful in keeping the two away from eachother, same with the possessed. For gnawers, I guess wards, but for posessed... maybe vampires would mistake them for demons or something if they're too overt. <br /> Mage? Well, I think the HIT mark V is dope, and more should be put in games. but mages are more than capable of avoiding vampires, or seeming like humans to vampires, so it's cool. <br /> <br /> From a werewolf perspective, mages are apparently after caerns, but i've never seen anyone implement such a scenario. My knowledge of mages is significantly less than that for werewolf and vampire. Now, the biggest problem for werewolves is that, well, they could easily off every vampire in the city without leaving much evidence. I guess banes might come out of vampire corpses, since they act like fly traps for banes, but there's a second rank theurge gift that lets you attack people from the umbra, and it has to <b>not exist </b>for anything to ever work. <br /> <br /> I'm a nutcase, and I'm really awaiting the vampire game where I can purchase my own hit mark or acquire a war wolf, but I'd never let players mix things up and I don't want the <i>other </i>to become familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:18:33-08:00","id":1178636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1175062#post1175062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Werewolf is 100% incompatible with Mage. Mage's conception of the cosmos is the exact opposite of what you find in Werewolf. You pick one or the other, and the one you don't pick ends up eating it..</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... I don't know... at most including Mage cosmology downplays the all-encompassing scale of Werewolf cosmology, but it doesn't negate it. It just makes it one paradigmatic viewpoint of a broader metaphysical conflict - especially if you embrace the idea of &quot;Telos&quot; as the 10th Sphere. The loss of Telos corresponds too perfectly to the binding of the the cycle of destruction, causing it to go mad.<br /> <br /> And of course that also fits with that event being the First Murder - if Ixion is Caine, then the event in question is the triumph of the farmer over the nomadic shepherd, so the Wyrm being caught in the Weaver's web and the loss of Telos was the neolithic revolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T20:38:21-08:00","id":1178660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1178636#post1178636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh... I don't know... at most including Mage cosmology downplays the all-encompassing scale of Werewolf cosmology, but it doesn't negate it. It just makes it one paradigmatic viewpoint of a broader metaphysical conflict - especially if you embrace the idea of &quot;Telos&quot; as the 10th Sphere. The loss of Telos corresponds too perfectly to the binding of the the cycle of destruction, causing it to go mad.<br /> <br /> And of course that also fits with that event being the First Murder - if Ixion is Caine, then the event in question is the triumph of the farmer over the nomadic shepherd, so the Wyrm being caught in the Weaver's web and the loss of Telos was the neolithic revolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you'rep laying with paradigms, you're in Mage-land, and nothing else is there but Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T20:55:39-08:00","id":1178663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1178660#post1178660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you'rep laying with paradigms, you're in Mage-land, and nothing else is there but Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That argument seems tautological to me. Of course a combined cosmology includes paradigms - it's combined, so it's going to include Mage's cosmology. As long as the Wyrm/Weaver/Wyld conflict is a real cosmological paradigm playing out in the Umbra, then Werewolf's cosmology is included as real. The problem only arises if you treat different cosmological paradigms as less than real. If you do that, then yes, Werewolf's cosmology becomes fake - but if you treat the different ways of interacting with the cosmos as all equally REAL, then it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:45:12-08:00","id":1178739,"title":"","content":"That's the deal with Mage...It doesn't &quot;negate&quot; stuff. It <b>relativizes</b> stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T09:31:00-08:00","id":1178827,"title":"","content":"I think I see what Saur Ops Specialist means. The problem with Mage is that it sets the Werewolf cosmology as one variable truth among many. Werewolf on the other hand is a game that relies on their cosmology as the fundamental underlying truth. Once you take that away, the game's underlying themes get lost. The Werewolves aren't desperate servants of Gaia fighting a likely doomed War to their last breath. They're misguided fanatics who've trapped themselves within a limited view of reality. It becomes a very different story.<br /> <br /> You can include Werewolf characters in a Mage game, or Mage characters in a Werewolf game. But I don't think you can give both settings equal weight. You've got to make the call: are Mages just creatures of the Trait with an imperfect understanding of their true place in Gaia's War? Or are the Garou just umbrood with delusions of grandeur who only think that they're dealing with an inevitable Apocalypse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 01-24-2018, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T10:24:11-08:00","id":1178855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1178827#post1178827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Werewolves aren't desperate servants of Gaia fighting a likely doomed War to their last breath. They're misguided fanatics who've trapped themselves within a limited view of reality. It becomes a very different story.<br /> the Garou just umbrood with delusions of grandeur who only think that they're dealing with an inevitable Apocalypse?</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here <i>is the truth </i>of werewolf though. Look at some of the tribebooks (particularly the shadow lords), the books of the other fera, even how elder vampires sum up why the lupines hate them. Note that galiards don't need honour, and nobody ever remembers the particular occasion that made the silver fangs the leaders. The garou have always been fighting a false war and they've always been believing their own BS, continuing on to make more. Werewolf's always been about the Rage, not the Gnosis, and every tribe has always been about what people personally think is more important and more importantly <i>their </i>issue. <br /> <br /> Of course, you should always run werewolf straight and ignore this knowledge till you really want to fuck with players who got way into buying the BS, but the game's a grim one once you strip away the power fantasy and the noble causes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T10:55:31-08:00","id":1178866,"title":"","content":"The &quot;noble cause&quot; is the core of setting, though. Whether or not the Garou are or had ever been worthy of that cause is an interesting question, but that doesn't change the way that Werewolf's objective reality forms the basis of the game.<br /> <br /> The tribes and Fera have different perspectives of the Garou's actions, understandably so, but they're generally all in agreement about a few things: the Triat exists. Gaia exists. Garou are intended to be the protectors of Gaia. The other Changing Breeds have their own specific roles. And there is a war, which the Garou are undeniably losing.<br /> <br /> (The perspective of elder vampires is a matter for Vampire the Masquerade, not Werewolf the Apocalypse. Obviously, it's something that should be addressed in a crossover game, but that's another matter of the storyteller and players choosing which splat's cosmology should be dominant in the game. It's another situation where the settings really can't be given equal weight, because there are too many direct contradictions.)<br /> <br /> It's particularly important when we look at things like the Impergium, the fall of the White Howlers, the fates of the Apis, Camazotz, Bunyip and others. Because it isn't just that the Garou have been responsible for monstrous things, but a lot of these deeds represent failures of their sacred duty on a much greater level. And these failures are part of why the Apocalypse seems inevitable today. (For example, the issue with the dwindling number of Garou might not be an issue at all if the Apis were still around to help matchmake.)<br /> <br /> These deeds don't carry the same meaning at all if we're looking at Garou history from the perspective of Mage's paradigms. What was a story about how the Garou's early arrogance and failure of their sacred duty may have led to their undoing simply becomes the story of Umbrood killing each other over their flawed interpretation of reality. We lose so much of the original nuance of the setting.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean people can't have fun playing a Garou in a universe with elements of Mage-cosmology, but it becomes a very different story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 01-24-2018, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T11:41:18-08:00","id":1178882,"title":"","content":"Indeed, Werewolves may be a bunch of murderous, even delusional, fanatics, but that's largely irrelevant to the underlying cosmology of the game.<br /> <br /> Werewolves may be wrong about many things. Perhaps Gaia isn't greater than the Triat. Perhaps they aren't the ones choosen to stop the Wyrm. Perhaps the Wyrm has to be released in order to restore balance. But the cosmic importance of the Wyrm, the spirit world, Apocalypse - these are never questioned. because that's the underlying theme of the game as much as the Jyhad it's the underlying theme of vampire.<br /> <br /> To say that Werewolf<i> entire cosmology</i> it's just a point of view (e.g: the Wyrm may be a comet, like Etherites say - sure, it's going to destroy the planet but no amount of ambientalism is going to stop it. That's their approach, as valid as Garou approach). This would be like saying that the Jyhad it's just paranoia (a lo &quot;fog of the ages&quot; in Requiem) or that mages are just mad people that live in a fixed reality and don't realize it. It ruins the game for a lot of people.<br /> <br /> It's not just a matter of &quot;truth&quot;, but of <i>purpose</i>.<br /> <br /> You can't very well depict the Ascencion War as &quot;the war to define Reality&quot; if you say that reality it's already defined. That's why a lot of mage fans complain when someone says that science would exist the same without the Technocracy. If the natural laws that science discovered are 100% objective, and Consensus can't change this, then there's no war for reality - there's one reality and a bunch of reality warpers that can't do meaningful chages to the world outside their small reach.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, if ALL what Garou have been doing it's just a PoV, then the spirit world looses a lot of it's importance - apeasing the spirits, traveling to the Umbra, figthing the Wyrm, are just your (outdated) way to deal with these issues - you could as well ignore the spiritual side of the game because that's a Paradigm. More so, all the &quot;dark&quot; aspects of Werewolf would be gone because the Impergium, the War of Rage, all the bad things Garou did, aren't really bad. They aren't bad because Garou believe they were necessary and belief shapes reality, remember - maybe they were necessary, if all PoV are equally valid so it's this one.<br /> <br /> Since these themes are very important, you need to thread carefully arround them (or just stomp them, with the blessing of your players, but that's not the theme of this thread).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-24-2018, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T12:09:55-08:00","id":1178892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1178855#post1178855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This right here <i>is the truth </i>of werewolf though. Look at some of the tribebooks (particularly the shadow lords), the books of the other fera, even how elder vampires sum up why the lupines hate them. Note that galiards don't need honour, and nobody ever remembers the particular occasion that made the silver fangs the leaders. The garou have always been fighting a false war and they've always been believing their own BS, continuing on to make more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in this context. They aggrandize their own achievements and this is why they haven't managed to make anything resembling peace with the Fera. Their enemies, however, are very real, and those enemies, Weavern Wyrm, or even Wyld sometimes, are coming at them and everything else for the exact reasons that you read in the book. The false tales here are the ones where the Garou are in the right for doing something dumb, and which you have to struggle through the hard way (not rising in Renown as quickly as rivals who don't question the old tales at all), not the fundamental assumption of the game (which both the Ahadi and Beast Courts back up; it is not solely a fight of the Garou Nation).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolf's always been about the Rage, not the Gnosis, and every tribe has always been about what people personally think is more important and more importantly <i>their </i>issue. </div> </div> </div>No. The Rage has always been something to keep you fighting when you need to use it. Using it all the time is a very well-established mistake, and the game itself will tell you this up-front in a number of places. Meanwhile, there's an entire chapter dedicated to spirits, the Umbra, and all the matters thereof.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, you should always run werewolf straight and ignore this knowledge till you really want to fuck with players who got way into buying the BS, but the game's a grim one once you strip away the power fantasy and the noble causes. </div> </div> </div>Not unless you want people to not play with you ever again. The switch is tolerable if it involves a dispute between Garou and Fera where the former wronged the latter but whitewashed it, but not when it comes to dealing with caern-robbing hermetic dipshits. You can pretty much splatter their heads and feel no or perhaps minimal guilt over it; they're just out to accumulate power for their own egos, and they have no cosmic insights worth noting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T15:31:54-08:00","id":1178972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1178827#post1178827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can include Werewolf characters in a Mage game, or Mage characters in a Werewolf game. But I don't think you can give both settings equal weight. You've got to make the call: are Mages just creatures of the Trait with an imperfect understanding of their true place in Gaia's War? Or are the Garou just umbrood with delusions of grandeur who only think that they're dealing with an inevitable Apocalypse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't their paradigm be capable of causing an apocalypse, even if it's just one paradigm among many?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:04:59-08:00","id":1178987,"title":"","content":"Besides some paradigms of the mages, like the one of the Euthanatos, is 100% compatible with the Gaian narration of reality.<br /> <br /> And guess around which Tradition does the mage metaplot focus on...?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Senex is sending me along to cabals all over North America to try to explain his intentions.<br /> The war is finished and the Wheel is crumbling. What does the Cycle do to compensate? It moves ever faster, toward a final conclusion. Senex has foreseen that the Lokha - all that is - will resolve itself in our lifretimes unless something is done.&quot;<br /> <br /> Janine lowers the cup from her lips. &quot;Resolve itself?&quot;<br /> &quot;End&quot; say Truce. &quot;The world's going to end.&quot;<br /> &quot;Not necessarily&quot; says Hetirck. &quot;He has a plan&quot;<br /> &quot;We are now the guardians of the Shade Realm of Entropy. Naraka Voormas knew how important it was; he planned to use it to flood the worlds with Jhor and bring about the end himself. That's why he sought out Earth's corrupt Nodes. Sympathetic ties between Earth and the Forbidden Lands of Helekar would let him channel the world-killing rite.&quot;<br /> <br /> I shake my head. More delusions of grandeur. &quot;Right, Chela Hetirck. I'm sure you would know all about Voormas'plans&quot;<br /> &quot;Intimately.&quot; Theora Hetirck doesn't bat an eye.<br /> So my voice goes up a tone. &quot;if it was a credible threat, why hadn't some sort of demon or Nephandus or something tried this before?&quot;<br /> &quot;Some of them were constrained to their own realms by cosmic laws. The others lacked the power.&quot;<br /> &quot;You don't mean that he could have -&quot;<br /> She gives the smallest nod.<br /> I have nothing to say.<br /> <br /> &quot;Senex's Madzimbabwe have been purifying the Nods that once strengthened Helekar. He believe that we can do the opposite of what Voormas intended. The power of the Forbidden Lands can reach through those Nodes and return the world to its proper balance, but it will take an army of awakened souls a long time to accomplish.&quot;<br /> &quot;How many of us?&quot; asks Truce, tapping a cigarette out of his pack.<br /> &quot;All of us&quot; says Hetirck. &quot;All of the Euthanatoi.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Can you believe this shit?&quot; I kick a flat rock aside. &quot;Mighty Senex wants us to abandon Earth so we can indulge his attempt to spin the Big Wheel? He's not my Guru, Truce. I don't have to liste to a goddamn thing he says&quot;<br /> &quot;You should have a Guru. I should have a Guru. I agree with him.&quot;<br /> &quot;I know what you mean. Bastard trips out past the Gauntlet and now he - &quot;Waitaminute. What did you say?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I agree with him. We can only do so much. You know janine's thing with the bridge? That's the world, Eve. We keep polishing and replacing the surface, but the supports are crumbling beneath us. There's just too much damage to repair the old way.&quot;<br /> &quot;Let me get this straight. You're saying that we've been wasting our time?&quot;<br /> He points to the sky. &quot;Look over there. Track down and to the right from Polaris&quot;<br /> &quot;I don't see anything.&quot;<br /> &quot;Look with Citta shight.&quot;<br /> <br /> I breathe, feel the flower open in my temple and look.<br /> The spirit-star is red of a bead of blood, swollen from the vein and ready to splash earthward.<br /> &quot;I've only read about it. This is the first time I've seen it myself.&quot;<br /> &quot;The signs are here. Akrites'Moloch. The rise of demons and dead things from the roots of the earth. Now this; the Ixos Folio calls it the Eye of Iblis.<br /> We followed the old ways, sowing and reaping souls with care and moderation - and it didn't work. Since the fall of Helekar and the Reckoning, real Gurus have been in short supply: technically we don't even constitute a genuine Chakra, you and I. How do we know that wiser people than ourselves haven't wanted us to change our ways before? Now we have a Chela from a real Guru - perhaps the only guru we can count on - telling us there's a new direction to take.<br /> How long do you want to play it safe, Evelyn? If this isn't a time for grand gestures - if this isn't the time to scourge the world - I don't know what is.&quot;<br /> &quot;So we just let the Sleepers wither on the vine?&quot;<br /> He grimaces and sweeps his arm toward the distant lights of Seattle. &quot;They had their change to redeem themselves and refused it! This is the Age of Kali. The prophecies tell us that they'll forget true dharma. In that respect they've proven to be literally correct. They treat the poor like pigs, the rich like gods, and grind their world underfoot.<br /> Fuck'em. I'll take Senex up on his offer and help his rite burn away the rot in the Wheel. Sleepers can either change their ways or get caught in the tide!&quot;<br /> &quot;You've got the Jhor running deep in you, Truce&quot;<br /> &quot;Don't I&quot; he says, marching for the door. &quot;Doesn't the world?&quot;<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-24-2018, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T06:16:29-08:00","id":1179168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead Rabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides some paradigms of the mages, like the one of the Euthanatos, is 100% compatible with the Gaian narration of reality.<br /> <br /> And guess around which Tradition does the mage metaplot focus on...?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>On the Order of Hermes.</b><br /> <br /> No ,really, it's on the Order of Hermes, those few paragraphs you mentioned aren't representative of the entire Mage Metaplot.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy formed with them. Gilgul was invented by them (see Heyel to see why this is important). Half the Traditions feelt pushed to the side because they are a bunch of dicks. Porthos was the narrator of the Fragile Path AND the one that started the fight against House Heleakar (Horizon Stronghold of Hope), by exposing their corruption to the Council (with the help of a young Hermetic) and forcing the Euthanatos to take action (they were putting the issue under the rug to not loose face within the Traditions). Porthos was the Archmaster that defended youth, saying that power was useless to achieve Ascencion and thus voicing many of the themes of the game. The Ascencion Warrior trilogy it's based on the fall of Doisettep and Horizon - which started Revised edition. House Janissary was also an important part of the plot, they were killed by the Euthanatos, but were part of the OoH (and some say that they faked their death, again). Also OoH are the ones that have crossovered the most. They fostered the Nine Spheres of Magick. They were the main force behind the legal system of the Traditions. They were the ones that pretty much leaded the Trads into the Ascencion War (the Traditions may have ended in Concordia when the Techocracy attacked the Grand Convocation if werent for the OoH and their dragons). Most of the stuff that happened in Mage it's either fault or omission of the OoH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-25-2018, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T06:54:00-08:00","id":1179176,"title":"","content":"Most books of Mage since the second edition follows Amanda and Senex. The ending of mage the Ascension is pretty much focused on the Euthanatoi, the whole scenario the Ascension is centered on Voormas and Senex. The Order of Hermes was the focus of mage in the first edition, after the second edition the Euthanatoi became the focus of the metaplot. Mage the Ascension as a setting doesn't end on Doissetep, ends on the battlements of the House of Helekar, on the shard realm of Entropy.<br /> <br /> Mage second edition,Book of the chantries, Book of the worlds, Book of Shadow,Book of Craft,Technomancer Toybox,and so on, the introduction of these books, and not only of these, are told from the point of view of Amanda.<br /> <br /> <br /> At this link there is a good summary of the metaplot, and it's clear that the writers have slowly but steadily diverted the focus of the metaplot on the Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.tenebrae-mundis.com/read.php?17,18688\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.tenebrae-mundis.com/read.php?17,18688\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.tenebrae-mundis.com/read.php?17,18688\" target=\"_blank\"> http://forum.tenebrae-mundis.com/read.php?17,18688 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-25-2018, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T09:08:31-08:00","id":1179221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most books of Mage since the second edition follows Amanda and Senex. The ending of mage the Ascension is pretty much focused on the Euthanatoi, the whole scenario the Ascension is centered on Voormas and Senex. The Order of Hermes was the focus of mage in the first edition, after the second edition the Euthanatoi became the focus of the metaplot. Mage the Ascension as a setting doesn't end on Doissetep, ends on the battlements of the House of Helekar, on the shard realm of Entropy.<br /> <br /> Mage second edition,Book of the chantries, Book of the worlds, Book of Shadow,Book of Craft,Technomancer Toybox,and so on, the introduction of these books, and not only of these, are told from the point of view of Amanda.<br /> <br /> <br /> At this link there is a good summary of the metaplot, and it's clear that the writers have slowly but steadily diverted the focus of the metaplot on the Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.tenebrae-mundis.com/read.php?17,18688\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.tenebrae-mundis.com/read.php?17,18688</a></div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't including Dark Ages and Cruzade in your analysis - Where Euthanatos are but a footnote because the action focuses on Europe - aka OoH. Also, I see plenty of mentions of the OoH in the 2nd edition section of your link, they did pretty important things (Doissettep, Janissary - their doings happens to be very important - more than Amanda sad story, that's for sure).<br /> <br /> Let's talk about Metaplot: The Plot it's what you do in your table as ST. The Metaplot, as it's name indicates, it's all of Mage's history that influences the world where you build the plot. Everything that was <i>important</i> in Mage History it's Metaplot, things like the foundation of the Technocracy and the Massa War are part of the Metaplot, they exists as an encompassing backstory for your plot. Amanda story it's but a very small part of the Metaplot even if a lot of fiction were written from her PoV.<br /> <br /> The Fall of Doissetep it's Metaplot, knowing about it I know about the Avatar Storm, the death of Porthos - OoH was there. The Founding of the Traditions it's Metaplot, knowing how it happened I can build stories - OoH was there. The Fall of Mistridge it's Metaplot. Everything I mentioned it's more foundational to the Metaplot of Mage than Amanda because they define how Mage society works, and thus inform how you play the game. OoH was <i>everywhere </i>in the Metaplot up to revised, and they influence the mood of the game a lot.<br /> <br /> Euthanatos barely did anything <i>important </i>with the exception of Vormass, and all his actions were to stop the Tenth Sphere. I remind you that the spheres are created/discovered following the Hermetic Paradigm. Voormas fighting Telos isn't a good defense for the Euthanatos Paradigm to be &quot;the truest Paradigm of mage&quot;. <hr /><br /> I want to add that the idea that Euthanatos Paradigm it's compatible with Werewolf it's plainly wrong. They don't relate to the Triad in the same way as Werewolf the Apocalypse does. For the Euthanatos the Triad it's more conceptual, they don't envision a massive cosmic war that's corrupting the world but rather a world that's getting more entropic thanks to the excesses of humanity. Again, the cosmic war thing it's very, VERY, important to Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Even if it was compatible, the very idea of a &quot;truest Paradigm&quot; it's anathema to Mage. Yet it's an idea that always comes up when you try to push Mage into Werewolf and doesn't work. Since Werewolf doesn't bulge to the Consensual Reality, let's destroy Mage instead, surely he can take it!. Well, no. Anything that pretends to prioritize one Paradigm of Mage over the others diminishes the importance of the Ascencion War. Suddenly you're supposed to use an Euthanatos cosmology regardless of the Consensus!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-25-2018, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T09:31:04-08:00","id":1179230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1111587-keeping-the-game-lines-separate?p=1178987#post1178987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides some paradigms of the mages, like the one of the Euthanatos, is 100% compatible with the Gaian narration of reality.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The concept of paradigms does not transfer to other games. The concept of consensual reality does not transfer to other games. If you start out talking about them, you're limiting your perspective to that of Mage, and ruling all other things out. Mage is not a GUT for the WoD; it is just another shard of it. Much as how Demon's layers of reality does not explain anything but how Demon works. It's not a GUT for a meta-setting WoD, either. These principles lean heavily on ignoring games that would contradict them directly. The only way you manage to join together games is by stitching in certain parts that can handle the stitching, and Mage has surprisingly few places where it actually accepts stitching from other settings, if any at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}